58,3,,status,George,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"The options are Paid Allocation, Shared Racks, or an Annual Lottery. Given the rain and the shoving matches, Shared Racks might be the most efficient, but we must consider the maintenance.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Paid Allocation would provide funds, but as Mio noted, the administrative burden and the risk of social division, as seen in the neighboring block, make it a risky choice.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,George,,"An Annual Lottery is the most neutral option. It addresses the stagnation I found in the minutes and ensures no one feels entitled to the best spots forever, without adding any cost.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Shared Racks would eliminate the ""ownership"" of spots and the shoving matches, but Mio's findings on the display frames suggest they are a physical and maintenance burden we can't afford.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Mio,,I'm really scared of the Shared Racks because of that maintenance! And Paid Allocation sounds like way too much paperwork. I think the Annual Lottery is the safest bet for everyone!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, I agree that the maintenance of racks is a concern, but a lottery doesn't fix the rain exposure or the morning congestion. However, it is the most realistic given our budget.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"If we prioritize stability and low overhead, the Annual Lottery is the most rational choice. Paid Allocation is too administratively heavy, and Shared Racks are physically impractical.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,George,,It seems we are reaching a consensus. The lottery is the only option that doesn't require a budget we don't have or a level of labor that would burn out our volunteers.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"I'll admit, while it doesn't solve the physical layout, it's the least likely to turn neighbors into enemies over money or broken equipment. I can get behind the lottery.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Mio,,Yay! I'm so glad we all agree. Let's go with the Annual Lottery so nobody has to do extra work and it stays fair for everyone!,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"I'll vote for the Annual Lottery. It's not a perfect physical solution, but it's the most equitable and sustainable option we have right now.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I also vote for the Annual Lottery. It is the most reasonable choice given our financial constraints and the administrative risks associated with the other options.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,George,,I vote for the Annual Lottery. It is the most straightforward way to ensure fairness and clear the long-standing stagnation in our parking assignments.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"I vote for the Annual Lottery. It's the most pragmatic way to avoid social friction and administrative headaches, even if it leaves some physical issues unresolved.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Mio,,I vote for the Annual Lottery too! It's the easiest for everyone and keeps things happy and fair!,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
